    "reasoningScore": 35,
    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Explain the influence of one-sided wording, including a prompt with opposing cost and agreement cues whose net effect cannot be assumed. This requires contextual interpretation of the taught leading-question category, rather than recalling a label alone."
  },
  "content": {
    "id": "p93-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Explain why the following survey questions may result in a biased statistical investigation.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p93-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Taking into account the budget deficit, should the government cut military expenditure?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p93-q1-a-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Leading question: mentioning the budget deficit may encourage support for cutting military expenditure.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "This is a leading question. The budget deficit supplies one-sided financial information before the question is asked. It directs attention towards saving money and may encourage respondents to support military spending cuts.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Taking into account the threat of Russia, should the government cut military expenditure?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p93-q1-b-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Leading question: mentioning a threat may encourage respondents to oppose cuts to military expenditure.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "This is a leading question. The reference to a threat supplies one-sided security information. It directs attention towards defence and may discourage respondents from supporting military spending cuts.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p93-q1-c-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Taking into account that the Sydney Metro is well over-budget, do you agree that we",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "should continue to fund it?",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p93-q1-c-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Leading wording: “well over-budget” may discourage funding, while “do you agree” may invite support. Their overall effect is not established.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The question presents one-sided cost information by emphasising that the project is “well over-budget”, which may discourage continued funding. However, “do you agree” may invite agreement with continuing to fund it. These features may influence responses in opposite directions; their overall effect is not established.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p93-q1-d-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The aging infrastructure of Sydney Trains has led to many major delays over the years.",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "What’s your opinion on the Metro project?",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p93-q1-d-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Leading question: negative information about Sydney Trains may encourage a favourable opinion of Metro as an alternative.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "This is a leading question. It presents negative information about the existing train system before asking about Metro. This one-sided context may make respondents view the existing system unfavourably and favour Metro as an alternative.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      }
    ]
  },
